---
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/,'');
import Documentation from '../layouts/Documentation.astro';
---
<Documentation title="Implementation"><main class="docs-catalogue"><h1>Implement the contract.</h1><p>Install only the packages your surface needs. All packages use the @klein-ui npm scope and ship TypeScript declarations.</p><pre><code>npm install @klein-ui/react @klein-ui/tokens @klein-ui/table @klein-ui/charts</code></pre><pre><code>{`import '@klein-ui/react/styles.css';
import '@klein-ui/forecast/styles.css'; // when using forecast
import '@klein-ui/eddy/styles.css'; // when using Eddy
import { Button, PageHeader } from '@klein-ui/react';`}</code></pre><p>Initial npm publication is pending maintainer authentication. Flowstate currently consumes the built packages as versioned tarballs through <code>npm run sync:klein</code>.</p><h2>Compose in order</h2><ol><li>Choose the page template and its scrolling boundary.</li><li>Use an existing organism for the task: a table, forecast, chart or conversation.</li><li>Use molecules and atoms only to fill documented slots.</li><li>Pass display-ready data and callbacks from the application.</li></ol><h2>Agent instructions</h2><p>Read the catalogue before writing JSX. Do not create alternate buttons, tabs, headers or tables. If a capability is missing, extend its canonical package with a typed example and behaviour test.</p><ul><li><a href={base+"/AGENTS.md"}>Consumer agent rules</a></li><li><a href={base+"/components.json"}>Machine-readable catalogue and examples</a></li><li><a href={base+"/props.json"}>Generated prop contracts</a></li><li><a href={base+"/compatibility.json"}>Migrated APIs</a></li><li><a href={base+"/migration.json"}>Source migration inventory</a></li></ul><p><a href="https://github.com/flowstate-oss/klein-design-system/blob/main/docs/RENDERER_AUDIT.md">Renderer ownership and retained application code</a></p><h2>Data belongs in the application</h2><p>Keep GraphQL, routing, saved-view persistence, authorization and calculations outside the library. Providers own presentation state; storage and URL adapters supply values and receive callbacks. Do not fetch from a component.</p><h2>Naming and composition</h2><p>Use value/onValueChange for composed selections and native onChange events for inputs. Public components use semantic variants and slots, not arbitrary CSS or vendor options. Tables is the product term; the complete collection includes its toolbar, state provider and renderer.</p></main></Documentation>
